#description: The use narrows the lineage's joinSchema with #J, declared beside the use, in a plain field rather than a definition. A narrowing may refer outside the lineage.
#expect: ok
#spec: docs/invariants.md:162-171
#at: lin.h
#known/fill-use: #264 the lineage is at the top of a root with no build instance whose files include the use's, so #J beside the use reads as declared in the lineage.
#known/unify-text-use: #264 the lineage is at the top of a root with no build instance whose files include the use's, so #J beside the use reads as declared in the lineage.
-- in.cue --
import "github.com/sdboyer/thema"

#J: {[string]: string, ...}
lin: h: thema.Lineage & {name: "h", joinSchema: #J}
-- text.cue --
schemas: "0": "0": schema: {a?: string}
-- out/fill-text-named/bind --
verdict: ok
-- out/fill-text/bind --
verdict: ok
-- out/fill-use/bind --
verdict: E0141
E0141 joinSchema refers to #J, which is declared in the lineage outside the joinSchema @ /m/in.cue:5:49
-- out/third-root/bind --
verdict: ok
-- out/together/bind --
verdict: ok
-- out/unify-text-use/bind --
verdict: E0141
E0141 joinSchema refers to #J, which is declared in the lineage outside the joinSchema @ /m/in.cue:5:49
-- out/unify-use-text/bind --
verdict: ok
